  "contract": [
    "Ordinary saved message/code/tool input and result copy uses canonical host-owned source, exact full displayed-message and logical-slot hashes, render-time provenance and one shared prepare/validate/clipboard path. Whole logical source is projected at its original rule root before code fence extraction or formatting.",
    "Usual default copy remains one click with no routine dialog. Per-action plaintext is an explicit secondary menu; it does not become a global default or authorize an unknown source. Protected unsupported media is refused; usable OFF and explicit canonical plaintext preserve original JSON.",
    "Unknown live/subagent DOM sources require host-authoritative usable OFF plus literal-only proof and final epoch/DOM/getter checks. Stale local OFF, paused OFF and ON plaintext cannot grant source/restoration authority.",
    "Log copy means the latest bounded host log-tail snapshot. Protected default retains only safe timestamp/status/ordinal with an omission notice; an explicit plaintext action is separate. Claimed session ids in logs confer no restoration authority.",
    "Boot copy always emits a fixed safe diagnostic summary, including when OFF or the host is unavailable. It never automatically selects raw diagnostics after failure. The full diagnostic remains locally visible; manual selection/Ctrl+C is outside the application-button contract.",
    "Callback/pairing capability and connector template copies retain their exact explicit management purpose. The generic clipboard reservation primitive itself grants no authority.",
    "Log helpers remain with the existing 04 logger owner; the abandoned new 00e module was removed. Existing module dependency policy was not relaxed."
  ],
